## Canonical data — referenced, never copied
- **Location:** {{DATA_LOCATION}}   *(`data/` read-only copy, or the resolved `data_path` pointer below)*
- **`data_path` (if off-tree):** {{DATA_PATH}}
- **Rule:** campaigns reference the data by **relative path** (`../../data`); the loop **never writes into
  `data/`** and **never copies** it into a campaign. This is what keeps the tree portable and duplication-free.

## Shared, promoted artifacts
`shared/` also holds artifacts a campaign froze that siblings consume (e.g. a validated forward model, a
generated training set) — each versioned. Downstream campaigns reference `../../shared/<artifact>`, never a
sibling's working folder. Current promoted artifacts: {{PROMOTED_ARTIFACTS}}

## Layout
`PROJECT.md` (this) · `LINEAGE.md` (index) · `DISCOVERIES.md` (promoted verified findings) ·
`ENGINEERING_NOTES.md` (durable "why"s) · `CLAUDE.md` (always-on rules) · `data/` · `shared/` ·
`campaigns/<name>/` · `sessions/<date>_<slug>/` · `reports/`. The whole tree relocates as one unit — all
internal references are relative.
